      },
      "worked": "Taking natural logarithms gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\n(\\ln a)\\ln(ax)&=(\\ln b)\\ln(bx)\\\\\n(\\ln a)(\\ln a+\\ln x)&=(\\ln b)(\\ln b+\\ln x)\\\\\n(\\ln a-\\ln b)\\ln x&=(\\ln b)^2-(\\ln a)^2\\\\\n(\\ln a-\\ln b)(\\ln x+\\ln a+\\ln b)&=0.\n\\end{align*}$$\nIf $a\\ne b$, then $\\ln a-\\ln b\\ne0$, so\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\ln x&=-\\ln a-\\ln b\\\\\n\\ln x&=\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{ab}\\right)\\\\\nx&=\\frac{1}{ab}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nIf $a=b$, the original equation has identical sides, so every $x>0$ is a solution.",
